### DocIQ API — quick manual smoke test (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP)
@base = http://localhost:4000

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### 1. Create a workspace
# @name ws
POST {{base}}/api/workspaces
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Acme Legal" }

### 2. Upload a document  (set workspaceId from the response above)
POST {{base}}/api/documents/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----b

------b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="workspaceId"

{{ws.response.body._id}}
------b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample-msa.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./backend/eval/fixtures/sample-msa.txt
------b--

### 3. Poll status  (set the document id)
GET {{base}}/api/documents/DOCUMENT_ID/status

### 4. Ask a question
POST {{base}}/api/query
Content-Type: application/json

{ "workspaceId": "{{ws.response.body._id}}", "question": "What is the termination notice period?" }

### 5. Risk / clause summary
GET {{base}}/api/documents/DOCUMENT_ID/risks

### 6. Update dynamic settings
PATCH {{base}}/api/workspaces/{{ws.response.body._id}}/settings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "topK": 8, "retrievalStrategy": "hybrid", "confidenceThreshold": 0.2 }

### 7. Query history
GET {{base}}/api/workspaces/{{ws.response.body._id}}/history
